Dry-fry @pine nuts{} or @flaked almonds{} in a #large pan{} until lightly toasted, then tip onto a plate. 

Add @olive oil{1%tbsp} to the pan, then fry @onion{1}(halved and sliced) and @cinnamon sticks{2}(broken in half) together until starting to turn golden. 

Turn up the heat, stir in @lamb neck fillet{500%g}(cubed), fry until the meat changes colour, then tip in @basmati rice{250%g} and cook for ~{1%minute}, stirring all the time. 

Pour in @water{500%ml}(boiling), crumble in @lamb stock cube{}, add @dried apricots{12}(ready-to-eat), then season to taste. 

Turn the heat down, cover and simmer for ~{12%minutes} until the rice is tender and the stock has been absorbed. 

Toss in the @pine nuts{} and @mint leaves{}(roughly chopped) and serve.